{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c523","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0abb3-41ff-7191-99eb-aba32c3c39db"},"sequence":236,"recorded_at":1780531400000467,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2dda60fb-bbf1-4b10-b11a-18e8803d4114","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"2dda60fb-bbf1-4b10-b11a-18e8803d4114","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2dda60fb-bbf1-4b10-b11a-18e8803d4114"},"call_id":"call_01a0abb40a7872fd8cb42f4fb8b387d1","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-4-1\",\n  \"command\": \"for f in /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-cr5.md /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_rework-rev5.md /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-cr6.md /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_rework-rev6.md; do echo \\\"===== $f =====\\\"; cat \\\"$f\\\"; echo; done\\ncat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev3.md | head -n 250\\necho \\\"=====verdict-rev4 head=====\\\"\\ncat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev4.md | head -n 250\",\n  \"description\": \"Read remaining reviewer and verdict docs\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"===== /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-cr5.md =====\\nIndependently review Change Request revision 5 of TASK-260909-2ez769 (task_delta on managed checkpoint a89328ca85a613abde39660f4be749a8fcf57903, candidate tree a823eb20be497c3fa0510e7da4d3506ddb284431, published by RUN-260916-c0f186). This is the rework after the CR4 changes-requested verdict (TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev4.md, evidence zip rev4); read that verdict, the CR4 logbook, the producer outcome TASK-260909-2ez769_results-rev5.md with TASK-260909-2ez769_producer-evidence-rev5.tar.gz and TASK-260909-2ez769_exclusion-handoff.md, the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes. Superseded reviewer briefs (reviewer, reviewer-current-base, reviewer-after-rev3, reviewer-after-rev3-current) are historical; this brief governs.\\n\\nThe producer ported the CR4 probes under new names (TestSurvivingReaderConvergesInterruptedApply, TestSurvivingReaderConvergesInterruptedRollback, TestFirstOpenPreservesHeldLock, TestConcurrentOpenAttachesToExistingLock) and claims a marker admission barrier in internal/hosttrust/joint.go and transact.go (markerPresent, convergeLocked, lockForConvergedRead), O_CREAT|O_EXCL / CREATE_NEW lock creation (FileSystem.CreateExclusive) with a 500ms verification budget, seven build-tagged Windows custody tests, TestApplyV4BackupIsClassifiedConfigCopy, a row-21 handoff with notes on seven owning tasks, 19 of 21 rows driven (rows 15 and 21 explicitly not driven), 25+1 hosttrust and 4+1 config plants killed with a neutral SURVIVED control and one documented converge-ignore survivor by the staged-marker backstop. These are producer claims requiring independent verification; in particular decide whether the shared-reader release-then-reacquire path leaves a window in which a second writer stages a new marker between the shared release and the exclusive acquisition, and whether the 500ms lock verification retry can admit a replaced inode. Verify the three CR4 findings against production entry points, RED-first evidence and your own isolated reproduction:\\nF1 (surviving-process admission): port or rerun TestReviewerCrashBetweenConfigAndGeneration and TestReviewerRollbackCrashSurvivingReader on the exact candidate; the surviving LoadCoherent must refuse or converge, never admit old generation 3/4; confirm the pending joint-commit marker is a general admission barrier across WithSharedSnapshot/readSnapshotLocked, readCommitted, authorization boundaries and mutation transactions, that stale requests are still refused (never silently refreshed), and that TestApplyV4CrashConvergesGeneration now asserts convergence with fatal expectations instead of returning silently on Load/Configuration/Open/ReadSnapshot errors. Cover apply and rollback, surviving and reopened processes, marker cleanup/error ordering. Distinguish tested refusal from proven recovery.\\nF2 (first-open lock replacement): rerun TestReviewerCrossProcessLockInitialization; with the child paused after the absence observation and the parent holding the lock, the child must end up on the same inode and must not return while the parent holds it; confirm initialization is atomic and non-replacing through production Open, that existing-lock contention is tested, and read the Windows initialization path for the same rule (report Windows execution honestly as unverified where no runtime ran).\\nF3 (evidence and ownership): native Windows DACL tests must exist as real build-tagged test code driving the production custody entries for owner-only acceptance, other-principal refusal and reparse handling; without a Windows runtime, row 15 is implementation present / runtime unverified, never a pass; config-backup contents must be classified against the applicable custody contract rather than profile-ACL inheritance; row 21 must carry a precise handoff naming each downstream owning task, API and test obligation (check the notes the producer wrote on those tasks) and be counted as not consumer-driven.\\n\\nRetain the CR3 repairs (stale generation refusal, same/separate-Store revocation contention) and the corrected config mutation accounting; re-derive the 21-row AC table from source and named tests, counting driven/bounded/failing rows honestly; check that every claimed exit comes from a real command status and that the harmless SURVIVED control was applied through the same harness; no compile-failure, unapplied or empty-selection kills. Confirm the parked RPC artifacts and control-root backup hashes are untouched and that no candidate path overlaps the RPC manifest; confirm checkpointed SSH/peer predecessors are preserved and no RPC transport was implemented.\\n\\nMethod: isolated immutable probes only (throwaway clone or extracted tree), never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local. Attach TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev5.md and TASK-260909-2ez769_review-evidence-rev5.zip, complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260909-2ez769, revision=5, evidence=TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev5.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2 classes and repeat-of named. Model: codex gpt-6-astra low. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.\\n\\n===== /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_rework-rev5.md =====\\nRework the credentials/Config4 candidate of TASK-260909-2ez769 after the CR5 independent changes-requested verdict by RUN-260916-f8925e (Astra low). Read TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev5.md, TASK-260909-2ez769_review-logbook-rev5.md and materialize TASK-260909-2ez769_review-evidence-rev5.zip (probe TestReviewerRestoreCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit, logs, mutation replay). Base is still the managed checkpoint a89328ca85a613abde39660f4be749a8fcf57903; CR5 candidate tree a823eb20be497c3fa0510e7da4d3506ddb284431 in the managed Story worktree .temp/STORY-260830-1kiyj6/worktree — continue from it. Preserve the checkpointed SSH/peer leaves, the parked RPC artifacts and the control-root backup with their recorded hashes; no RPC transport; no manual commits; no direct .task-board edits; no self-acceptance. Superseded briefs (producer, rework-rev3, rework-rev4) are scope context only; this brief governs.\\n\\nThe CR5 finding is the third consecutive verdict in the crash/coherence transaction family (CR3 crash-transaction, CR4 surviving readers, CR5 unlocked error compensation): each rework closed the witnessed seam and left the next mutation path outside the lock. Do not fix restoreSourceAfterJointFailure as one more seam. First build the instrument that closes the class: a write-path census of every code path that creates, replaces, removes or renames config.json, its backups, trust.json, the pending joint-commit marker, the lock file and the credential files — apply, rollback, restore-after-joint-failure, Recover/convergeLocked, Initialize, JointCommit leftover handling, Enroll/Rotate/Revoke/MarkRetiring, backup publication, and any helper (writeTempReplace, replaceDurably, secureStaged, CreateExclusive) — as a table with, per row: the production call site, the lock state it requires (exclusive with converged intent / shared fast path / none), the intent revalidation it performs before writing (current generation, marker state, exact preview/source), the positive test, the interleaving negative (a surviving reader or another writer completing or superseding the operation between the failure and the compensation), and the narrowing plant. Enforce the census with a gate that fails when a filesystem mutation of the pair happens outside a held exclusive authorization: either a static gate over the hosttrust/config packages (every caller of the replace/remove helpers must be reachable only from a lock-held context, with a control plant that proves the gate sees a new unlocked caller) or a runtime assertion in the helpers keyed to the lock holder, with a behavioral test for each row. Attach the census as TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev6.md.\\n\\nThen repair F1 against the census: error compensation after a failed JointCommit (apply and rollback) must run inside the same authorization transaction or reacquire the exclusive lock and revalidate the exact intent (pending marker state, current generation, configuration bytes/digest) before choosing a converged outcome; if another process completed, superseded or converged the operation, the compensation must not restore the old configuration — it refuses or adopts the converged state with the generation change intact. Port TestReviewerRestoreCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit RED first (the seam that turns trust.json to 0644 so custody validation refuses the trust commit, then a surviving LoadCoherent converges to Config4/generation 4, then the failed writer resumes), keep it as a committed test, and add deterministic production tests for apply and rollback trust-commit failures racing (a) a surviving reader, (b) another writer, (c) a held boundary. Keep the CR4 repairs green (surviving-reader convergence, first-open lock preservation, stale-generation refusal, revocation contention) and re-run the original seven reviewer probes. Note the reviewer bound on verifyLockFile's 500ms retry (custody rechecked, inode not pinned): document it as a stated bound or pin the inode, but do not claim protection against an owner replacing lock files externally unless you implement it.\\n\\nRetain rows 15 and 21 exactly as CR5 accounted them (Windows native tests present, runtime unverified; matcher-only, consumer handoff persisted); do not inflate them. Update the 21-row AC matrix with actual calls and named tests; rerun the hosttrust and config mutation batteries on the exact final source with per-plant raw logs, a neutral SURVIVED control applied through the same harness, exits from subprocess return codes, and no compile-failure/unapplied/empty-selection kills. Full configured local validation before the normal producer handoff; no hosted CI. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first. Leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED for the handoff snapshot. Attach TASK-260909-2ez769_results-rev6.md, TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev6.md and TASK-260909-2ez769_producer-evidence-rev6.tar.gz, then hand off through task-board and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be codex gpt-6-astra low.\\n\\n===== /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-cr6.md =====\\nIndependently review Change Request revision 6 of TASK-260909-2ez769 (task_delta on managed checkpoint a89328ca85a613abde39660f4be749a8fcf57903, candidate tree b0bb3d9d600d4c323aa12480b3285512f96167c7, published by RUN-260916-44fc4f, 55 changed paths). This is the rework after the CR5 changes-requested verdict (TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev5.md, review-evidence-rev5.zip, review-logbook-rev5.md): read that verdict, the producer outcome TASK-260909-2ez769_results-rev6.md, the census TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev6.md, TASK-260909-2ez769_producer-evidence-rev6.tar.gz, the rev6 patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes. Superseded reviewer briefs (reviewer-cr5 and earlier) are historical; this brief governs.\\n\\nCR3, CR4 and CR5 were one family — a config/trust pair mutation outside the authorization transaction — so review the instrument first: the census must enumerate every production path that creates, replaces, removes or renames config.toml, its backups, trust.json, the pending joint-commit marker, the lock file and the credential files (the producer claims 12 rows) with lock state, intent revalidation, positive test, interleaving negative and narrowing plant; verify completeness against the source with your own walk (every caller of writeTempReplace, replaceDurably, secureStaged, CreateExclusive, os.Rename/Remove/Create in internal/config and internal/hosttrust), and verify that TestWritePathCensusGate actually sees a new unlocked caller (plant your own rogue caller in an isolated copy in a shape the producer's three control plants did not use — a new file, a method receiver, a var-bound helper — and confirm the gate fails). An undriven or uncensused row is a finding.\\n\\nThen verify the CR5 F1 repair: JointCommit now takes the restore closure and compensates under the same exclusive hold (compensateLocked: marker re-read and pin-compared, configuration hash equal to the replacement pin, restore, restored bytes re-read against the source pin, marker abort; committed trust deliberately not re-read), the unlocked restoreSourceAfterJointFailure is deleted, ErrJointReplacementDurable reports a clean abort and ErrJointCompensationFailed reports failed compensation with the marker kept. Rerun TestReviewerRestoreCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit on the exact candidate (the producer says its seam now blocks on flock; confirm that the final state can no longer be the CR5 failure and that the port TestApplyV4CompensationCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit asserts the final state), and probe the six compensation race tests for apply and rollback against a surviving reader, another writer and a held boundary; decide whether \\\"never re-read committed trust\\\" can abort a bump that actually became durable and whether that is a safe refusal or a silent loss. Keep the seven original reviewer probes green.\\n\\nRetain rows 15 and 21 exactly as CR5 accounted them (Windows native tests present, runtime unverified; matcher-only, consumer handoff persisted); re-derive the 21-row AC table from source and named tests; check that the hosttrust (29+1 kills, neutral SURVIVED) and config batteries report exits from subprocess return codes with per-plant raw logs and no compile-failure/unapplied/empty-selection kills; confirm RPC backup 15/15 and parked 11/11 hashes and zero overlap with the candidate; confirm checkpointed SSH/peer predecessors are preserved and no RPC transport was implemented.\\n\\nMethod: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local. Attach TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev6.md and TASK-260909-2ez769_review-evidence-rev6.zip, complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260909-2ez769, revision=6, evidence=TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev6.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2 classes and repeat-of named. Model: codex gpt-6-astra low. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.\\n\\n===== /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_rework-rev6.md =====\\nRework the credentials/Config4 candidate of TASK-260909-2ez769 after the CR6 independent changes-requested verdict by RUN-260916-c3e675 (Astra low). Read TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev6.md, TASK-260909-2ez769_review-logbook-rev6.md and materialize TASK-260909-2ez769_review-evidence-rev6.zip (probes TestReviewerLegacyCannotOverwriteCommittedV4, TestReviewerFailedReplacementCannotLoseIntent, TestReviewerFailedRollbackCannotLoseIntent, TestReviewerRoguePlantExecutes with the four plant files, logs). Base is still the managed checkpoint a89328ca85a613abde39660f4be749a8fcf57903; CR6 candidate tree b0bb3d9d600d4c323aa12480b3285512f96167c7 in .temp/STORY-260830-1kiyj6/worktree — continue from it. Preserve the checkpointed SSH/peer leaves, the parked RPC artifacts and the control-root backup with their recorded hashes; no RPC transport; no manual commits; no direct .task-board edits; no self-acceptance. Superseded briefs are scope context only; this brief governs.\\n\\nThis is the fourth consecutive verdict in the config/trust transaction family (CR3, CR4, CR5, CR6), and CR6 shows the census instrument itself is not closing the class: the census exempted the legacy migrate writer (row 10) and the static gate detected 1 of 4 executable unlocked writers. Fix the instrument at the type level, not by adding names to a list: every helper that creates, replaces, removes or renames config.toml, its backups, trust.json, the pending joint-commit marker or the credential files must require an unexported exclusive-hold capability value that only the authorization lock acquisition path can construct (for example a *heldExclusive token returned by the lock and passed into writeTempReplace/replaceDurably/secureStaged/marker helpers and the raw os.Rename/Remove/Create call sites, all of which move behind that token), so an unlocked writer cannot compile; keep the static census gate as the second line and make it symbol-aware or fail-closed: unresolved writer references, package-level var-bound function literals, local aliases of the helpers, method receivers and os-qualified selectors reached through wrappers must all be violations unless the call site is one of the censused definitions, with the four reviewer plants (direct FuncDecl, package var function literal, local-variable alias, method receiver via wrapper calling os.Rename) plus your own fifth shape committed as executable controls that must fail the gate; document any writer that legitimately runs without the lock (credential fresh-key directories, lock creation) as a censused row with a proof that it cannot touch the committed pair.\\n\\nThen repair the two P1 rows against the census: F1 the legacy migrate path (internal/config/migration.go migrate) must run inside the authorization transaction with source revalidation under the lock (or refuse once any Config4 pair has been committed), so a delayed legacy Rename can never overwrite an admitted Config4 at an unchanged generation — port TestReviewerLegacyCannotOverwriteCommittedV4 RED first and keep it; F2 a failed replacement must never discard intent: JointCommit must not remove the pending marker on a replace error without proving from source/replacement pins which state is on disk; when the replacement rename succeeded and restoration failed, keep the marker (or converge forward) so readers refuse or converge instead of admitting a changed configuration at the old generation — port TestReviewerFailedReplacementCannotLoseIntent and TestReviewerFailedRollbackCannotLoseIntent RED first, cover apply and rollback, surviving readers and reopen, and keep the CR5 compensation races, the seven original probes and the CR4 repairs green.\\n\\nRetain rows 15 and 21 exactly as CR5/CR6 accounted them; update the 21-row AC matrix with actual calls and named tests; rerun the hosttrust and config mutation batteries on the exact final source with per-plant raw logs, a neutral SURVIVED control through the same harness, exits from subprocess return codes, and no compile-failure/unapplied/empty-selection kills; add narrowing plants for the token gate (a helper that accepts a nil token) and for both repaired rows. Full configured local validation before the normal producer handoff; no hosted CI. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first. Budget: the run has 4 hours and the runtime's own 26-command validation suite runs after your handoff, so hand off no later than 3 hours in; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED. Attach TASK-260909-2ez769_results-rev7.md, TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev7.md and TASK-260909-2ez769_producer-evidence-rev7.tar.gz, then hand off through task-board and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be codex gpt-6-astra low.\\n\\n# CR revision 3 review — changes requested\\n\\nTask TASK-260909-2ez769; CR-TASK-260909-2ez769-3 revision 3.\\nBase a89328ca85a613abde39660f4be749a8fcf57903; candidate tree\\n881fb127162ee55a0175313850b4704f41cb24e0. Review is read-only against the\\nmanaged worktree. Probes and overlays ran in an archive of the immutable tree\\nunder .temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/review3. No commits or product edits.\\n\\n## Blocking findings\\n\\n1. **P1: stale mutation authorization is admitted.**\\n   `internal/hosttrust/authorize.go:191`, `WithMutationAuthorization`, replaces\\n   the request generation with current.Generation and never compares the\\n   original binding. `TestReviewerStaleMutation` opens an authorized fixture,\\n   commits a config authorization generation change, then submits the original\\n   request. It returns nil and invokes the side-effect callback. Exit 1.\\n   Section 11.10.3 expressly forbids refreshing a cached number to authorize\\n   old prepared work. Refuse stale requests before entering the boundary;\\n   require fresh connection/replanning through the RPC caller contract. Add a\\n   negative test and a narrowing mutant for this mutation path, not only the\\n   dispatch generation guard.\\n\\n2. **P1: revocation succeeds during an authorized mutation boundary.**\\n   `internal/hosttrust/lock_unix.go:60-73` uses flock on the same open descriptor\\n   for all goroutines of a Store, without process-local serialization.\\n   `TestReviewerRevocationDuringBoundary` waits until the production mutation\\n   callback is held, then calls Revoke on that Store. Revoke returns success\\n   before the callback is released. Exit 1 on darwin/arm64.\\n   The existing `TestMutationAuthorizationSerializesWithRevocation` uses an\\n   immediate nonblocking select after starting the revocation goroutine; it\\n   does not give that goroutine time to attempt the lock and misses the bug.\\n   Implement safe local and cross-process locking, including nested reads and\\n   concurrent lock initialization; test deterministic boundary contention.\\n   Section 11.10.3 forbids this success ordering.\\n\\n3. **P1: config replacement and generation commit are not crash-atomic.**\\n   `internal/config/migration_v4_apply.go:82` installs configuration inside\\n   `CommitConfigChange`; `internal/hosttrust/transact.go:87` commits trust only\\n   after the callback. Recovery is an in-process error handler, with no durable\\n   joint transaction/restart marker. `TestReviewerCrashBetweenConfigAndGeneration`\\n   drives production apply with an OS filesystem wrapper and terminates the\\n   child process with exit 77 immediately after the real config rename. On\\n   restart, production Load accepts Config4 and a freshly opened Store accepts\\n   the old generation (3). The parent test fails, exit 1. No synthetic trust\\n   bytes or fake decoder are used. This is a process-crash ordering test, not a\\n   power-loss filesystem test. Sections 6.6 and 11.10.3 require the coherent\\n   committed config/trust transaction. Add durable recovery/selection and\\n   corresponding apply/rollback crash tests. Also move current-preview/source/\\n   generation revalidation into the shared transaction: presently those checks\\n   precede lock acquisition, leaving a concurrent-change window. The latter\\n   window is code-inspection evidence, not a separately executed probe.\\n\\n4. **P1: native Windows custody is not implemented to its required contract.**\\n   `internal/hosttrust/custody_windows.go:11-42` requests only owner SID and\\n   equates it with owner-only access. Ownership does not establish DACL grants;\\n   no DACL is read or installed. Common permission checks additionally apply\\n   Unix 0700/0600 tests before this function, without a Windows ACL abstraction.\\n   Sections 11.10.2 and the explicit native-Windows platform lanes require\\n   equivalent owner-only ACLs. A successful cross-build and an absent Windows\\n   runner cannot waive the implementation requirement. Implement and validate\\n   ACL custody (positive owner-only and negative other-principal access/reparse\\n   cases). No Windows execution was performed here; actual Windows runtime\\n   acceptance/refusal remains unverified, not claimed as observed leakage.\\n\\n5. **P2: no-secret replication and complete negative-coverage claims exceed evidence.**\\n   `ExcludedFromReplication` has no production consumer; its only caller is\\n   `TestExcludedFromReplication`. `TestNoSecretReplication` walks the local\\n   custody directory and asserts file placement; it does not drive replication,\\n   snapshot, clone, Session Directory or diagnostic export. No actual secret\\n   leak is claimed, but the mandatory exclusion is not established at those\\n   entry points. Provide production enforcement/negative tests or an explicit\\n   scoped ownership handoff for unavailable surfaces; do not count a returned\\n   path list as end-to-end exclusion. The config `v4-explicit-label` mutant\\n   changes only the error identity while retaining refusal: its kill proves\\n   label precision, not a narrowed semantic admission gate. Correct the claim\\n   of four config narrowing kills to three semantic plants plus one label plant.\\n\\n## Independently derived AC accounting\\n\\n**18 of 21 functional AC rows driven**, including three rows with failing\\nreviewer counterexamples. This is a functional decomposition of sections 6.6,\\n11.10.2 and 11.10.3 within this leaf, not a claim of all normative clauses or\\nall gate mutants covered. Fifteen rows have bounded passing test evidence;\\nthree rows below lack the required production proof. The producer's unlisted\\n21/21 does not establish complete acceptance.\\n\\n| # | Scoped row | Production call / named test | Result or bound |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n|1|Closed Config4|Decode / TestDecodeConfiguration4Refusals|Driven, passes|\\n|2|Historical compatibility and explicit migration|Migrate / TestMigrateRefusesV4Target, TestMigrateRefusesV4Downgrade|Driven, passes|\\n|3|Closed trust document|DecodeTrust / TestDecodeTrustRefusals|Driven, passes|\\n|4|Missing/corrupt trust refuses|ReadSnapshot / TestReadSnapshotMissingStore, TestCorruptTrustRefusedNeverEmpty|Driven, passes|\\n|5|Fresh issuance|IssueCredential / TestIssueCredentialProfile|Driven, passes|\\n|6|Exact profile and time bounds|VerifyProfile / TestVerifyProfileRefusals, TestVerifyProfileRefusesJustPastExpiry|Driven, passes|\\n|7|Explicit tuple enrollment|Store.Enroll / TestEnrollRefusals|Driven, passes; OOB human verification remains operator act|\\n|8|Mapping uniqueness|DecodeTrust / TestDecodeTrustRefusals duplicate-root/key rows|Driven, passes|\\n|9|Rotation/retirement bounds|Rotate, MarkRetiring / TestRotateBoundedWindow, TestMarkRetiringCapsAtLeafExpiry|Driven, passes|\\n|10|Revocation tombstones|Revoke, Enroll / TestRevokeTombstone, TestRevokedLeafNeverReenrolls|Driven, passes serially|\\n|11|Old-generation mutation refusal|WithMutationAuthorization / TestReviewerStaleMutation|Driven, FAIL|\\n|12|Boundary/revoke serialization|WithMutationAuthorization, Revoke / TestReviewerRevocationDuringBoundary|Driven, FAIL|\\n|13|Coherent config plus trust snapshot|ReadSnapshot returns trust only; caller supplies allowlist|Not established; missing combined production proof|\\n|14|Unix owner custody|Open, ValidateCustody / TestCustodyRefusals, TestValidateCustodyBindsDirectory|Driven on Darwin, passes|\\n|15|Windows equivalent ACLs|verifyOwner|Not driven; implementation gap F4|\\n|16|Complete peers and selected credential|PreviewV4 / TestPreviewV4PeerEnrollment, TestPreviewV4CredentialGates|Driven, passes|\\n|17|Exact preview and confirmation|ApplyV4 / TestApplyV4PreviewMismatch, TestApplyV4ConfirmRequiredWithDrops|Driven, passes serially|\\n|18|Current source/generation apply|ApplyV4 / TestApplyV4StaleSource, TestApplyV4StaleGeneration|Driven, passes serially; transaction window remains|\\n|19|Crash-durable config/trust pair|applyV4, Load, ReadSnapshot / TestReviewerCrashBetweenConfigAndGeneration|Driven, FAIL|\\n|20|Explicit backup rollback|RollbackV4 / TestRollbackV4, TestRollbackV4BackupGates|Driven, passes normal/error paths; stopping channels belongs to RPC/operator boundary|\\n|21|Secret exclusion across export surfaces|ExcludedFromReplication, local walk only|Not production-driven across required surfaces|\\n\\nLive TLS/handshake/dispatch admission and one-second stream closure remain the\\nRPC task's scope, not a newly invented guarantee of this leaf. Peer distribution\\nis operator duty. No blanket waiver for custody, generation or crash atomicity.\\n\\n## Verification and provenance\\n\\n- Reviewed supplied producer results, retry2, retry3, refresh and CR validation.\\n- Independently verified base includes adoption trunk 8cf4aaa; base signature\\n  verifies as oparin@me.com. Candidate archive contains the v0.6.0 adoption.\\n- Patch SHA256 matches a1ee1e7dd2120ce8bb883d55ad3092bd53c46432e7791ddc2c8bf30334266d81.\\n- RPC backups 15/15 and parked untracked files 11/11 match manifest hashes;\\n  none of those paths overlaps the 44-path CR. RPC preservation resource remains\\n  attached to TASK-260830-z1yxg9. No checkpointed SSH/peer changes were modified.\\n- Reran immutable config/hosttrust/peeridentity package tests with -count=1\\n  -cover: exit 0; coverage 93.2%, 77.0%, 97.5%. Initial live-tree run also exit 0;\\n  acceptance conclusions use the immutable archive run. An intermediate masked\\n  run passed but is superseded by the complete three-package rerun.\\n- Accepted whole-repository build/vet/full-suite and publication validation from\\n  the attached rev3 log rather than rerunning unrelated gates. Those green\\n  checks do not override the three new negative failures.\\n- Reran four semantic narrowing overlays: stale-direction, custody-0644,\\n  preview-length, confirm-drops, each exit 1 with the expected named failing\\n  test. Two neutral controls pass exit 0. Harnesses exit 0. Probe sources were\\n  moved out of package test discovery before these control/mutant runs.\\n- Independently checked producer mutation source SHA256 manifests against the\\n  immutable archive: 25 hosttrust files and 7 config files match. Retained\\n  producer results record 15 hosttrust kills, 3 config semantic kills plus\\n  1 label kill, and two passing controls. This is not every-gate coverage.\\n- New probes fail exit 1 (hosttrust two tests; config crash test). Child crash\\n  exit 77 is asserted by its parent. Evidence archive preserves source, logs,\\n  commands/exit accounting, mutation outputs and provenance verification script.\\n- Readiness: Go 1.25.5 darwin/arm64, git 2.50.1, Python 3; task-board mutation\\n  succeeded. Managed worktree lacks local skill adapters; required Curator Go\\n  skill was read from the main checkout's managed symlink. Initial missing-path\\n  and unknown resources-query attempts were corrected without installing tools.\\n\\n## Routing\\n\\nRequest developer rework, status to-dev. No acceptance, commit_ack, integration,\\ncommit or main push. Keep preservation and current managed base intact. Attach\\nthis verdict and the reproduction evidence before ending the reviewer run.\\n=====verdict-rev4 head=====\\n# Revision 4 review: changes requested\\n\\nTASK-260909-2ez769 / CR-TASK-260909-2ez769-4 revision 4.\\nBase: a89328ca85a613abde39660f4be749a8fcf57903.\\nCandidate tree: 2c8909c9c7425bb3a90c00b8db3762f43b4dbf39.\\nReview against an immutable archive; no managed-worktree product edits, commits, integration or landing.\\n\\n## Blocking findings\\n\\n### F1 — P1: surviving processes accept an interrupted config/trust pair\\n\\n`internal/hosttrust/transact.go`, `WithSharedSnapshot`/`readSnapshotLocked`, and\\n`internal/hosttrust/authorize.go`, `readCommitted`, never inspect the pending\\njoint-commit marker. Recovery happens only in `Open` (or explicit `Recover`).\\nThe exclusive OS lock disappears when the writer crashes, but other processes\\nwith already-open Stores remain alive and can acquire it and read old trust\\nalongside the replaced configuration. Locking alone does not make that pair a\\ncommitted pair. The same omission reaches authorization and ordinary trust\\ntransactions; the marker is not a general admission barrier.\\n\\nExecuted real child-process probes against the candidate:\\n\\n- `TestReviewerCrashBetweenConfigAndGeneration`: production `applyV4` exits 77\\n  after the real config rename; surviving parent's production `LoadCoherent`\\n  succeeds with the replaced configuration and generation 3 (the old value).\\n  Parent test FAIL, go test exit 1.\\n- `TestReviewerRollbackCrashSurvivingReader`: first performs real `ApplyV4`, then\\n  production `rollbackV4` child exits 77 at the replacement seam; surviving\\n  `LoadCoherent` succeeds with generation 4 (the old value). FAIL, exit 1.\\n- `TestReviewerCrashReopenConverges`: a fresh `Open` after the apply crash does\\n  converge and passes with fatal assertions on read/open errors. This repair\\n  works for new openers, but does not cover surviving processes.\\n\\nRepair all read/admission/transaction entry points under the authorization lock\\nso unresolved intent is recovered or refused before exposing a snapshot or\\nrunning a boundary. Cover both apply and rollback, surviving processes as well\\nas reopen, and marker cleanup/error ordering. Do not silently refresh a stale\\nrequest to the recovered generation. Section 11.10.3 requires coherent committed\\nreads across processes, not just after reopening a Store.\\n\\nThe shipped `TestApplyV4CrashConvergesGeneration` still returns success early on\\nLoad, Configuration, Open and ReadSnapshot errors (migration_v4_apply_test.go,\\nroughly lines 419–436). Those branches cannot prove successful convergence.\\nReplace them with explicit expectations, distinguishing a tested refusal from\\nsuccessful recovery. No shipped rollback child-crash test was found.\\n\\n### F2 — P1: concurrent first-open replaces a held authorization lock\\n\\n`internal/hosttrust/lock_unix.go`, `openLock`, uses Lstat-absent followed by\\nCreateTemp and replacing Rename. `lockInitMu` serializes only goroutines in one\\nprocess. Two processes can both observe absence; the delayed process renames\\nits staged lock over the first process's already-held lock. Subsequent locks\\nthen attach to a different inode and no longer serialize.\\n\\n`TestReviewerCrossProcessLockInitialization` deterministically pauses a real\\nchild's production `openStore` after its absent-lock Lstat. Parent `Open` creates\\nthe lock, initializes trust and holds an exclusive acquisition. Releasing the\\nchild allows its `Open` to finish while the parent still holds the old lock.\\nThe test verifies both facts: `returnedWhileHeld=true sameInode=false`.\\nFAIL, exit 1 on Darwin/arm64. Only the filesystem observation is synchronized;\\ncreation, rename, Open and locking are production code against OS files.\\n\\nUse atomic non-replacing lock initialization shared by all processes; never\\nreplace a live lock inode. Exercise concurrent first-open and existing-lock\\ncontention through production entry points. Inspect the analogous Windows\\ninitialization path too. Do not infer a native Windows failure from this Darwin\\nexecution.\\n\\n### F3 — P2: remaining acceptance/evidence claims exceed their reach\\n\\n- Native Windows DACL read/install code now exists; CR3's owner-SID-only\\n  implementation criticism is no longer accurate. However `TestOwnerOnlyGrants`\\n  is a pure evaluator and cross-build/vet do not execute native owner-only,\\n  other-principal or reparse acceptance/refusal. There are no native Windows\\n  tests in the candidate. Row 15 is not production-driven. No observed leak is\\n  claimed. Add the native tests and actual platform evidence required by scope;\\n  accurately retain unavailable runtime evidence as unverified.\\n- The config writer stages backups using Chmod only; the producer expressly\\n  leaves Windows backup DACLs to profile inheritance. The direct 11.10.2\\n  owner-only clause governs credential custody, so I do not assert every plain\\n  configuration backup is a leaked private key. Still, inherited profile ACLs\\n  are not evidence of owner-only access. Classify the actual backup contents\\n  and applicable contract rather than claiming this bound proves custody.\\n- `MatchExcludedFromReplication` and `ExcludedConfigDirName` still have only\\n  test callers. The outcome supplies a generic future-consumer instruction,\\n  but no named owning downstream task or corresponding attached API/test\\n  handoff. Implemented matcher tests are useful and public enrollment remains\\n  separate; they do not establish exclusion through replication/snapshot/clone/\\n  Session Directory/diagnostic consumers. Persist the precise ownership handoff\\n  for unavailable consumers, as CR3 F5 permits, and count row 21 honestly.\\n- Config label-precision mutation accounting was corrected. Retain that fix.\\n  Three newly affected hosttrust narrowing plants fail the expected named tests,\\n  and the applied harmless control survives. These do not cover F1/F2.\\n\\n## Independent AC accounting\\n\\n**19 of 21 functional AC rows driven**, of which 16 have bounded passing\\ncandidate evidence and 3 have failing reviewer counterexamples. Rows 15 and 21\\nare not driven at the required native/consumer entry points. This is the same\\n21-row functional decomposition used in CR3, not a claim of every normative\\nclause or every gate covered. A driven row can fail.\\n\\n| # | Row | Production call / named test | Result |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n|1|Closed Config4|Decode / TestDecodeConfiguration4Refusals|Pass|\\n|2|Historical compatibility, explicit migration|Migrate / TestMigrateRefusesV4Target, TestMigrateRefusesV4Downgrade|Pass|\\n|3|Closed trust document|DecodeTrust / TestDecodeTrustRefusals|Pass|\\n|4|Missing/corrupt trust|ReadSnapshot / TestReadSnapshotMissingStore, TestCorruptTrustRefusedNeverEmpty|Pass, ordinary paths|\\n|5|Fresh issuance|IssueCredential / TestIssueCredentialProfile|Pass|\\n|6|Profile/time bounds|VerifyProfile / TestVerifyProfileRefusals, TestVerifyProfileRefusesJustPastExpiry|Pass|\\n|7|Explicit enrollment|Store.Enroll / TestEnrollRefusals|Pass; OOB verification remains operator act|\\n|8|Unique mapping|DecodeTrust / TestDecodeTrustRefusals duplicate-root/key cases|Pass|\\n|9|Rotation/retirement|Rotate, MarkRetiring / TestRotateBoundedWindow, TestMarkRetiringCapsAtLeafExpiry|Pass|\\n|10|Revocation tombstones|Revoke, Enroll / TestRevokeTombstone, TestRevokedLeafNeverReenrolls|Pass, serial paths|\\n|11|Stale mutation refusal|WithMutationAuthorization / TestReviewerStaleMutation|Pass, repaired|\\n|12|Shared authorization serialization|Open/openLock / TestReviewerCrossProcessLockInitialization; WithMutationAuthorization/Revoke / TestReviewerRevocationDuringBoundary and TestReviewerSeparateStoreRevocationDuringBoundary|FAIL first-open; existing same/separate-Store contention passes|\\n|13|Coherent config/trust readers|LoadCoherent / TestReviewerCrashBetweenConfigAndGeneration, TestReviewerRollbackCrashSurvivingReader|FAIL surviving readers|\\n|14|Unix custody|Open, ValidateCustody / TestCustodyRefusals, TestValidateCustodyBindsDirectory|Pass on Darwin|\\n|15|Windows equivalent ACLs|verifyOwner/installOwnerOnlyACL; only TestOwnerOnlyGrants model test|Not native-driven|\\n|16|Complete peers/local credential|PreviewV4 / TestPreviewV4PeerEnrollment, TestPreviewV4CredentialGates|Pass|\\n|17|Exact preview/confirmation|ApplyV4 / TestApplyV4PreviewMismatch, TestApplyV4ConfirmRequiredWithDrops|Pass|\\n|18|Current source/generation apply|ApplyV4 / TestApplyV4StaleSource, TestApplyV4StaleGeneration|Pass; in-lock helper tests additionally present|\\n|19|Crash-durable pair/recovery|applyV4, rollbackV4, LoadCoherent / reviewer crash tests above|FAIL surviving readers; fresh apply reopen passes|\\n|20|Explicit rollback|RollbackV4 / TestRollbackV4, TestRollbackV4BackupGates|Pass ordinary/error paths; crash bound in row19|\\n|21|Secret exclusion across consumers|MatchExcludedFromReplication/ExcludedConfigDirName / helper tests only|Not consumer-driven; precise ownership handoff incomplete|\\n\\nRPC handshake, actual dispatch, watchdog and operator distri\\n[tool output bounded: strategy=head, original_bytes=42172, visible_bytes=40000]\\n<system-reminder>\\nFull output saved to: /Users/iv/.local/share/muse/sessions/2026/09/16/01a0abb3-41ff-7191-99eb-aba32c3c39db/tool-outputs/01a0abb4-112e-70a0-a3d3-e4041c4ac5cc/call_01a0abb40a7872fd8cb42f4fb8b387d1-bash.txt\\nFull output is longer than the visible window.\\nUse bash tools like head, tail, cat, sed, or grep to inspect and search the full output.\\n</system-reminder>\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 42172,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 10543,\n  \"truncated\": true\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
