{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e17b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0abb3-41ff-7191-99eb-aba32c3c39db"},"sequence":3864,"recorded_at":1780531400007723,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2dda60fb-bbf1-4b10-b11a-18e8803d4114","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"2dda60fb-bbf1-4b10-b11a-18e8803d4114","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2dda60fb-bbf1-4b10-b11a-18e8803d4114"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0abe5-adae-79f2-bbcf-025ba97845e1"},"task_id":"01a0abe5-adae-79f2-bbcf-025ba97845e1","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0abe5-adae-79f2-bbcf-025ba97845e1","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-94-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -n 40 LOGBOOK.md; echo ...; tail -n 20 LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Check logbook format\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-16\\n\\n### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev6 — CR5 unlocked-compensation finding repaired as a class\\n- F1: `JointCommit` takes the restore closure and compensates a failed bump under the SAME exclusive hold (`compensateLocked`): marker re-read pin-for-pin, config hash must equal the replacement pin, restore result verified against the source pin before the abort. No reader/writer/boundary can converge between failure and restore. The unlocked `restoreSourceAfterJointFailure` is deleted. Original CR5 probe RED (exit 1, quoted failure) pre-fix; post-fix its in-seam convergence blocks in `flock` (timeout dump proves the hold) and the ported `TestApplyV4CompensationCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit` pins the race as goroutine-vs-gated-restore.\\n- CENSUS: 12-row write-path census (`TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev6.md` board outcome) covers every pair mutation incl. legacy `migrate` (fail-closed row, pinned by `TestLegacyMigrateBesideMarkerRefusesConvergence`), inert credential staging, atomic lock creation, and the sabotage remainder (vanished-marker re-stage). Enforced by committed static gate `TestWritePathCensusGate` + control `TestWritePathGateFlagsUnlockedCaller`; preserve-token order-swap plant `compensate-verify-before-restore` passes the gate and fails only behaviorally.\\n- INTERLEAVINGS: 6 deterministic gated-restore race tests (apply/rollback × reader/writer/held-boundary) + 2 production-entry clean-abort tests + 8 hosttrust compensation tests (tamper/corrupt/unreadable marker, noop+wrong-bytes restore verification, fail-after-write, source-present skip). TEST BUG FOUND BY RACE SUITE ITSELF: boundary tests deadlocked reading trust post-seam on the main goroutine — request now binds pre-seam with a comment.\\n- EVIDENCE: hosttrust battery 29 narrowing (incl. 4 compensate-*) + 1 call-site + neutral passed; config 6 semantic + 1 label + neutral passed; all plants pre-verified count==1 with exits from subprocess return codes. Full local CI replicated green (26 ok, 0 FAIL, 1 pre-existing SKIP; race 26 ok; cover hosttrust 77.9/config 93.3; tracecheck/catalog-6/cigate-contracts-6/claims-6/targets-2/fuzz-13/fixtures 51+59 zero-skip/windows-compile). 7 original reviewer probes re-pass; rows 15/21 retained bounded per CR5.\\n- BOUNDS RESTATED: verifyLockFile 500ms retry rechecks custody without pinning an inode (no external-replacement claim); power-loss beyond fsync unproven; Windows runtime unverified; diagnostics export unowned; spurious-bump corner aborts fail-safe.\\n\\n### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev5 — CR4 surviving-reader + lock-init findings repaired\\n- F1: pending joint-commit marker is now a general admission barrier (`convergeLocked` + shared-to-exclusive dance `lockForConvergedRead`): every read/admission/transaction entry point converges or refuses before exposing a snapshot. Surviving stores converge exactly like reopened ones; stale bindings compare against the recovered generation (never refreshed). Real child-process crash tests (exit 77) cover surviving + reopened × apply + rollback, marker cleanup, and intervened refusal with marker kept.\\n- F2: lock init is atomic non-replacing (O_CREAT|O_EXCL / CREATE_NEW via `FileSystem.CreateExclusive`); losers open the existing inode. Existing-file verify retries 500ms for the create-to-secure window; non-regular refuses immediately. Deterministic cross-process first-open test pins returnedWhileHeld=false + sameInode=true; the replacing-rename mutant restores the exact reviewer failure shape.\\n- F3: native Windows custody tests written (7, build-tagged; vet + test-compile pass, runtime unverified); config backups classified (byte-exact config copies, 0600, excluded names; Windows backup DACLs a stated bound); row-21 handoff persisted with per-surface API/test obligations + notes on all 7 owned tasks, diagnostics explicitly unowned.\\n- MUTANT LESSON: a JointCommit converge-ignore mutant survives because the staged-marker refusal backstops it — error-ignoring mutants are unobservable where a file-level backstop stands. Paired instead: joint-converge-skip (call-site, killed) + recover-forward-no-bump (narrowing, kills 8 named convergence tests).\\n- EVIDENCE: hosttrust battery 25 narrowing + 1 call-site killed + neutral passed; config 4 semantic + 1 label + neutral passed; full local CI replicated green (test/race/cover/tracecheck/catalog/cigate/fuzz-13/fixtures/claims/windows-compile). 19 of 21 AC rows driven; rows 15 (Windows runtime) and 21 (consumers) bounded, not passed.\\n\\n## 2026-09-10 (refresh)\\n\\n### TASK-260909-2ez769 refresh — story base moved c1eff01 to a89328c (trunk 8cf4aaa + v0.6.0 adoption)\\n- REFRESH: `task-board worktree refresh-candidate` with exclusive lease (RUN-260910-a4ac2c). Round 1 (43c0e2b peer-identity): 5 file resolutions — LOGBOOK merged newest-first, README trunk + peer tail, 3 traceability files trunk-wins (v0.6.0 registry pin authoritative; v0.5.0 digest superseded). Round 2 (c1eff01 SSH): 4 resolutions reusing round-1 bytes + README with SSH `## SSH stdio transport` section appended and peer-section wording. Packet schema learned from tool errors: entries {checkpoint_oid, path, sha256, content-base64}. Both replayed commits signed oparin@me.com (41106b6, a89328c, verify-commit Good).\\n- COMBINE: worktree restored to candidate snapshot by tool; 30 enumerated incoming paths restored from HEAD (8 adoption files incl. SPEC.v0.6.0.md, v0.6.0.lock.json, ownership.v0.6.0.json, task-board.config.json v0.6.0 cataloggen command); 6 tracked candidate files untouched by adoption kept; LOGBOOK re-merged (HEAD + 2 prior credential entries). Candidate bytes verified 40/40 match pre-refresh fingerprint.\\n- INTEGRATION (real semantic conflicts, resolved preserving both intents): adoption tests pinned \\\"v4 reader unimplemented\\\" — now stale. `compatibility_regression_test.go` const Version4 removed (production wins, same value); v4 lanes now positive per-lane loads (windows/ax.conpty, wsl2/ax.tmux, native plugdirs); conpty-on-v4 now closed-shape refusal (ErrConfigDecode, never version refusal). `schema_test.go` v4 branch now bare-doc required-member refusal + complete-doc positive (SourceVersion 4.0.0, ssh_tls13, host_channel); \\\"unsupported major\\\" renamed. `migration_test.go` assessor now 6 read-only / 10 compatible / 0 refused (was 6/6/4). `migration_refusal_test.go` v4 row now wants ErrMigrationV4Explicit (explicit-preview gate pinned through adoption test).\\n- VALIDATION (head a89328c): gofmt clean; go vet ./... clean; GOOS=windows build hosttrust+config ok; go build ./... ok; go test ./... -count=1 26/26 ok; -cover config 93.2 hosttrust 77.0 peeridentity 97.5 secprim 94.4; tracecheck ok (63/36/101/32, clauses 17/463); catalog v0.6.0 -check ok (former gate-21 input present). Mutation batteries rerun on new base: hosttrust 15 narrowing killed + neutral passed; config 4 narrowing killed + neutral passed; manifests bound to a89328c in mutations-hosttrust-refresh/ and mutations-config-refresh/.\\n- PRESERVATION: RPC backup 15/15 manifest match; parked 11/11 match; tracked RPC paths clean; no rpcwire/UNRESOLVED remnants; RPC delta absent from candidate. Worktree left UNCOMMITTED for snapshot; no main push/integration (orchestrator step).\\n\\n## 2026-09-10 (later)\\n\\n### TASK-260909-2ez769 retry — closed-reader hardening + mutation refresh\\n- SCOPE: same candidate; new gates only in `internal/hosttrust` + 1 census row. No config-package behavior change.\\n- FINDING: `DecodeTrust` never bound identifiers to bytes (crafted/corrupt store with swapped digests decoded) and never checked cross-entry leaf/key/root uniqueness at read time; fixed in `trust_decode.go`/`trust.go` with 5 new refusal rows.\\n- FINDING: `MarkRetiring` (peer catch-up path) missed the no-later-than-old-leaf-expiry cap that `Rotate` enforces; added with `TestMarkRetiringCapsAtLeafExpiry`.\\n- FINDING: `ValidateCustody` never bound the contained leaf to the credential directory name (valid credential filed under another name passed); added digest-vs-dir check with `TestValidateCustodyBindsDirectory`.\\n- FINDING: old `unsorted entries` refusal fixture was malformed JSON (refused on shape, never reached the ordering check); replaced with a genuinely descending valid pair. The `>=`-to-`>` sort mutant stopped killing once the mapping gate subsumed identical entries; re-aimed to `==` (admits unsorted-but-distinct) killing via the genuine fixture.\\n- FINDING: `AuthorizeDispatch` doc overclaimed same-lock check+dispatch; corrected to the actual guarantee (coherent check under shared lock; caller binds generation + watchdog; mutations use exclusive `WithMutationAuthorization`). Stale `transact` missing-store comment and `TOML/JSON` error comment fixed.\\n- VALIDATION (this run): `go build ./...` 0; `go vet` touched pkgs 0; `gofmt` clean; `go test ./... -count=1` all ok; `go test ./... -cover` all ok (hosttrust 77.0%, config 93.2%, peeridentity 97.5%, secprim 94.4%); hosttrust harness 15 narrowing killed + neutral passed; config harness 4 killed + neutral passed; census + refusal-inventory green.\\n...\\n- FIX (identity): `identityGatesInSyntax` now derives `bytes.Equal` calls and visits package-level var initializers under their variable name (same scope rule as the constructor census; per-scope ordinals keep all existing rows identical). One live row added: `context.go|CheckContextEcho|bytes.Equal(received.raw, sent.raw)` (domain `context-echo`, driver `TestCheckContextEcho`) — the live instance rev6 named. Header enumerates 8 identity-decision shapes (7 derived, 1 bound: other stdlib predicates) and qualifies the census sentence to derived shapes.\\n- FIX (bound): `boundSitesInSyntax` visits package-level var initializers and derives guards over length variables bound directly from `len(...)`/`stringLength(...)` (parens/conversions unwrap; `values := make(..., len(x))` binds no variable — proven by synthetic negative), plus direct `stringLength(...)` comparisons. Four live mechanism half-rows added (checkStringBounds + checkSortedUniqueStrings enforcements, exempt with caller-row drivers). Header enumerates 10 bound shapes (6 derived, 2 stated-pinned, 2 bounded: decoded-value comparisons with live checkUint53Bounds:269, direct cap/RuneCount with none live) and folds in the 21 refusal-side-only drivers instead of claiming min/max admission per site.\\n- FIX (constructor): no derivation change (7/7 already); header enumerates the 7 construction shapes with residue (frameFault-via-alias, non-Go construction, out-of-dir/_test.go), plus synthetic proofs for failX in return/argument/struct-field positions and returned `axerror.New`.\\n- FINDINGS (battery corrected the work, all in-session): the first length-var rule (RHS subtree contains len) over-derived on `values := make([]T, 0, len(elements))`, claiming element sortedness checks as len sites — tightened to direct binding; the P7 switch-arm plant kills at the arm witness entry, not the switch census (statement-vs-arm division of labor, now stated in the header); capability-clause and mechanism-comparison narrowings always co-fire their census by exact-render design — reported as behavioural kills with expected co-fire, never as clean singles.\\n- EVIDENCE: 15-row battery, 6 behavioural kills (incl. echo same-length narrowing failing `TestCheckContextEcho`, mechanism max+1 failing 5 bound suites, conditional-at-write-gate failing `TestCheckTargetWriteGatesRefusesNonAvailableEnabled`), 6 census-only kills (all three rev6 plant shapes now redden), 3 stated survivors green (plain-param bound, cap, reflect.DeepEqual). Tables attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-table-rev7.md`, narrative as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_rework-evidence-rev7.md`.\\n- SCOPE: test files only (`identity_census_test.go`, `bound_census_test.go`, `inventory_test.go`) + LOGBOOK.md (this entry); zero production changes. `go test ./...` 17/17 green, vet + GOOS=windows vet + gofmt clean, `-race` green, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=88). Census counts: identity 100 (86/14), bound 107 (80/27), constructors 7; test inventory 109->111 (+2 synthetic, 0 removed).\\n- STATUS: handed to review, work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n\\n## 2026-09-10 (later)\\n\\n### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework — CR3 changes-requested repaired on base a89328c\\n- SCOPE: same candidate, no base move (adoption trunk already in). All five CR3 findings addressed in `internal/hosttrust` + `internal/config`; no RPC absorption (4 tracked RPC paths verified CLEAN, parked 11/11 intact, no rpcwire remnants).\\n- P1 STALE MUTATION: `WithMutationAuthorization` no longer refreshes the cached generation; a binding older than committed refuses `ErrStaleGeneration` (`authorize.go`). Committed `TestWithMutationAuthorizationRefusesStaleGeneration` + narrowing plant `stale-mutation-refresh` (KILLED).\\n- P1 BOUNDARY/REVOKE: lock descriptors are per-acquisition (unix `flock`, Windows `LockFileEx`), so same-process goroutines serialize like separate processes; lock-file creation guarded by a process mutex; `Initialize` no longer re-acquires (unlocked nested read + documented no-reentry discipline). Existing serialization test hardened to the deterministic 250ms contention shape. Narrowing coverage via `revoke-state` + serialization tests.\\n- P1 CRASH ATOMICITY: new joint commit (`joint.go`): closed `PendingCommit` marker, `JointCommit` (in-lock revalidation + marker + replace + bump + unmark), `Recover` (forward/abort/refuse) auto-run by `Open`. `CommitConfigChange` removed (it encoded the split-brain pattern). Apply/rollback revalidate preview/source/generation/custody inside the exclusive hold; post-bump failures restore source + converge via `Recover` (`ErrJointReplacementDurable`). Committed real child-process crash test (`TestApplyV4CrashConvergesGeneration`, exit 77) plus abort/intervention/already-bumped/exhaustion unit tests. Power-loss vs process-crash documented honestly (fsync-durable, disk-dependent).\\n- P1 WINDOWS DACL: `verifyOwner` now audits owner SID plus every DACL allow entry (null/empty/deny-only/unknown-type fail closed); creation paths install protected owner-only DACLs (`secureStaged`); Unix mode checks abstracted via `platformModeOK` (exact 0700/0600 preserved). Pure `ownerOnlyGrants` evaluator tested on darwin (9 cases). No Windows runner exists here: evidence is GOOS=windows build + vet clean, unit tests, and an explicit stated bound (no invented runtime pass).\\n- P2 EXCLUSION: `ExcludedFromReplication` gains the joint marker; new `MatchExcludedFromReplication` (staging prefixes, fail-closed escapes) and `ExcludedConfigDirName` (.bak./.pre-rollback./.ax-config-*) with custody-walk + published-backup-name tests. No in-repo replication/snapshot/export-of-state surface exists (sessadapter/localstore/dirnode do not touch host-channel); outcome hands consumers + required tests to future export surfaces. Config claim corrected: 4 semantic narrowing + 1 label-precision kill (label plant marked LABEL-PRECISION in-table).\\n- ROW 13: new production `LoadCoherent` (config+trust under one shared hold) + serialization test.\\n- VALIDATION (rerun this run, exit 0): gofmt clean; `go vet ./...`; `go test ./... -count=1` all ok (281 top-level PASS across hosttrust/config/peeridentity/secprim); `-cover` hosttrust 77.8 config 93.1 peeridentity 97.5 secprim 94.4; `-race` on hosttrust+config ok; tracecheck ok; catalog v0.6.0 -check ok; linux+windows amd64 builds ok; `git diff --check` clean; refusal-inventory audit green (new sites covered by direct revalidation/helper tests); census green. Mutation batteries rerun exact-source: hosttrust 18 narrowing KILLED + neutral passed; config 4 semantic + 1 label KILLED + neutral passed (manifests bound to a89328c in mutations-*-rework/).\\n- STATUS: ready for review, worktree UNCOMMITTED for handoff snapshot. `task-board validate` shows 231 pre-existing board-wide ledger-mirror issues, none referencing this task.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 16050,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 4013,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
